<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">One ERP for Clinic, Pharmacy &amp; Finance</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            BasaRx is not a pharmacy bolt-on. It is the healthcare operating layer of the Pindah
            platform — where dispensing, EHR, stock, POS, and the general ledger share the same
            documents, patients, and products.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">What “integrated” means in practice</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Inventory:</strong> Dispense deducts stock and batch via FEFO, scoped by
            location and till, then invalidates caches so counters see truth. Procurement,
            transfers, and stock takes supply the same catalogue clinicians and pharmacists search.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Accounting &amp; POS:</strong> Dispenses post sale and COGS. Payments create
            receipts. Shortfalls queue to POS with live signalling. Multi-currency tills and
            payment methods match Zimbabwe’s operating reality.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Patients &amp; CRM:</strong> One customer/patient record carries allergies,
            medical aid, and history into both counter and consulting room.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Clinic EMR:</strong> Prescriptions, encounters, appointments, admissions,
            labs, and surgery bookings link to invoices — clinical events become billable events
            without re-keying.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Insurance:</strong> Claims and remittances attach to the same financial
            documents as retail and hospital pharmacy.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-0">
            <strong>Logistics (optional):</strong> Verified dispenses hand off to home-delivery
            trips with special-handling tags (Fridge, Urgent, Chemo, and more), OTP/signature/photo
            proof of delivery, and rider apps — clinic → pharmacy → door without a second patient ID.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Permanent business numbers, real documents</h2>
        <p>
            Scripts and invoices use domain prefixes (<code>RX-</code> for dispenses,
            <code>Rx-</code> for clinical prescriptions) from the moment of create. Draft or
            pending is a <em>status</em>, not a temporary number scheme. That keeps labels,
            notifications, pickup counters, and audit trails aligned for the life of the document.
        </p>
        <p>
            Prescriptions and dispenses are first-class financial documents on the shared invoice
            ledger — which is why stock, claims, and GL stay coherent without nightly sync jobs.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
